From a460eea965893de45fda33f8013c89b0f25829fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:52:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Name the draws, make the result card a dialog, stop the dots
 before five seconds

- The rules dialog on both pages now says a game can end in stalemate or by
  threefold repetition; the engine did both and the cards named both while
  the rules said nothing. test/rules-copy.test.js keeps the pages agreeing.
- The result card is role="dialog" and Escape dismisses it, returning focus
  to the board. It is still not modal: "See that move" reads the board
  behind it. The selected square carries aria-selected.
- The waiting dots run three loops under both motion settings (3.3s and
  4.5s), under the five seconds after which WCAG 2.2.2 wants a pause
  control; the status text keeps saying "Listening". DECISIONS.md says what
  replaced the earlier reasoning.

Verified in Chromium: Escape hides the overlay and focuses the board,
aria-selected="true" on the chosen square, computed iteration count 3 under
both settings, and the sentence renders in the dialog. CACHE v44 -> v45.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
