-are hidden outright once no relay answers, so nothing implies progress on a search that has stalled.
+Under `reduce` those dots animate **only their opacity** — a cross-fade carries no vestibular risk
+and is the substitution Apple's own guidance names. Reduced motion means no movement, not a dead
+indicator. They are hidden outright once no relay answers, so nothing implies progress on a search
+that has stalled.
+
+**The dots stop after three loops, under both settings** (3.3s bouncing, 4.5s cross-fading). WCAG
+2.2.2 asks for a way to pause anything that moves for more than five seconds beside other content,
+and the dots sit beside the link field and two buttons; the "essential" exemption is for a loading
+phase during which nothing can be interacted with, which this is not. The earlier reasoning here —
+that the one card whose job is to say "still listening" should keep saying it — is carried by the
+status text, which keeps saying it after the dots come to rest.
 
 Verified in Chromium under both settings by sampling computed `opacity` and `transform` over ~1.1s:
 nine distinct transforms under `no-preference`, exactly one under `reduce`. A rule in the sheet is
@@ -252,6 +259,20 @@ one-way latency per move" understated it. Guarded by `test/clock.test.js`, which
 over eighty plies at 250ms latency and asserts the two views never part by more than the tolerance,
 and by `test/shell.test.js`. **Not verified with two real peers** — nothing in this sandbox can be.
 
+### The result card is a dialog that is not modal
+
+`role="dialog"`, focus moves into it when it arrives, and **Escape dismisses it** (sets
+`resultDismissed`, returns focus to the board). It is deliberately not `showModal()`: the loss card's
+own "See that move" reads the board behind it, and a modal would make that board inert. Before this
+it was a `role="group"` that took focus and could not be closed from the keyboard — the shape of a
+dialog without the contract. The selected square also carries `aria-selected`.
+
+### The rules name the draws
+
+Stalemate and threefold repetition end games — 13 of 16 self-play games at the Learning level — and
+the dialog said nothing about either while the result cards named both. One sentence in the
+"things that trip people up" section, identical on both pages, guarded by `test/rules-copy.test.js`.
+
 ### The end of a match is announced by focus, not by the toast
 
 When the overlay arrives, focus moves to `.result-card` — `tabindex="-1"`, named by its headline and
@@ -405,6 +426,8 @@ Honest list of what is not done and what cannot be checked from a sandbox:
 
